<title>ITALY: Italy's Milan sees March CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Milan sees March CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Milan said its March consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 2.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In February Milan's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 2.6 percent respectively. The general index and housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of an Italian court decision last month to suspend electricity tariff cuts.</p>
<p>Milan is one of 11 Italian cities to publish CPI data on Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 19.1 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to February 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0     (0.2R)  2.2   (2.6R)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3    (-0.4)   0.7   (1.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1     (0.2)   3.2   (3.8)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.5    (-0.4R)  9.5   (9.1R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.1     (0.5)   2.1   (2.2)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.3     (0.6)   3.4   (3.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.4     (0.0)   0.5   (0.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.4     (0.3)   0.0   (0.4)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.1     (0.2)   4.1   (4.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0     (0.5)   2.8   (3.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2     (0.5)   1.3   (1.3)</p>
<p>R - Revised.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
